// WO INT-4A: M4 UI wiring -- sketch profile -> extrude/revolve -> boolean ->
// STEP export, entirely through visible UI affordances, reachable in the
// real app via mountLab3DPage.ts's `?lab3d=1&workbench=1` branch (NOT a
// dev-server-only demo URL -- see that file's header). Every dialog follows
// the SAME framework contract src/components/model3d/tree/demo/ChassisDemo.tsx
// (WO UI-3's evidence harness) already proved: FeatureDag holds the document,
// RegenScheduler drives each dirty feature's kernel op, CommandHistory gives
// undo/redo for free through InsertNodeCommand/EditFeaturePayloadCommand.
//
// Reconciliation strategy: after every history mutation (dialog Apply, undo,
// redo) this page disposes any kernel body/sketch outline whose DAG node no
// longer exists, then marks ONLY the changed node dirty (WO INT-4A-R1,
// R1.3 -- docs/3d-modeling-plan.md:221's "dirty-marking from the edited node
// downstream only") and lets RegenScheduler's own downstream-closure walk
// (regen/scheduler.ts's markDirty) expand that to exactly the dependents
// that actually need to re-run. Undo/redo don't get a command-supplied id
// for free (CommandHistory doesn't expose which node a popped command
// touched), so this page keeps its own touched-id past/future stacks in
// lockstep with CommandHistory's -- the SAME acknowledged limitation and
// established fix params/table.ts's ParameterTable already uses (see its
// own touchedPast/touchedFuture comment). Undoing a node's genesis INSERT
// removes it entirely; per that same file's genesis-undo cascade, this page
// then re-drives the removed node's former direct consumers instead (there
// usually are none in this WO's demo scale, but the mechanism is real).

// WO UI-17 (criterion 1, the cohesion root cause): the workbench route mounts
// INSTEAD of the app (mountLab3DPage.ts), so App.tsx's global stylesheet
// imports never ran here -- every CAM class this page referenced (.modal-btn,
// dialog chrome) rendered unstyled and every var(--...) fell back to its
// inline literal. Importing the SAME two sheets App.tsx imports is what makes
// "visually match the main software" possible at all.
